  id: W1_00
  era: "c. 1.5 million years ago \u2013 321 BCE"
  title: Ancient India
  text: 'Ancient India. From the first toolmakers to the early kingdoms. Some of the oldest stone tools in South Asia, about 1.5 million years old, come from Attirampakkam near Chennai. Over hundreds of thousands of years people here became farmers and then city-builders: by 2600 BCE the Indus Civilisation had planned cities with drains, standard weights and a script that is still undeciphered. After its decline came the age of the Vedas and, by the sixth century BCE, kingdoms, coins and new religions.'
  narration: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d02b3baf064104d6ab7fd20a3484917b, type: 3}
